  "implemented": [
    "Planning retains original image reference, alt and title without resolving resources. A revision-bound opaque preparation handle validates snapshotted bytes through the host decode port before native execution.",
    "New and retained paragraphs, native headings, existing table paragraphs, registered containers and entirely new tables materialize Word pictures, embedded media, locked inline controls and exact source payloads in one native history transaction.",
    "Image reservations resolve their final native paragraph and offsets after other staged operations. The same transaction owns actual drawing IDs, relationship IDs, binary parts and payload identity.",
    "Standard main parts use public withEmbeddedImage. Nonstandard owner folders author correct media relationship targets initially through public binary and relationship primitives. Post-mint canonical relationship rewrites are not used.",
    "Only newly inserted images resolve and allocate media. Later surrounding text edits retain existing picture identities, fingerprints, source payloads and bytes.",
    "The Apache detached Markdown exporter accepts caller-owned imageAssets. Managed image projection uses native drawing occurrences and exact source spans, preserving adjacent hyperlink syntax. Default and unregistered drawing projection remain omitted/protected.",
    "Standard syntax is used only when exact reference, alt and title survive normalization. Reserved literal image data syntax retains other values, including empty titles, whitespace, Unicode and GFM pipes.",
    "Eight test-only shared transport cases cover both client orders, both reconnect receivers and standard/custom main parts. Distinct valid PNG bytes and native blip relationship traversal prove independent media binding through both actor histories, peer text, caret geometry, exact Word fingerprints and DOCX/room reopening."
  ],
